From 42639128cc9be7c3afcb509bbd2aa40da3be2e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:24:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: preflight secure contexts before
 programming

A secure restore failure after allocating page-table ops leaves an
unpublished allocation behind. If a later context fails, earlier contexts
may already reference the unpublished domain. Complete all fallible secure
initialization before programming any context, release the unpublished
table on failure and clear both domain association pointers.

The release operation also exists in the cached official IOMMU next tree
2cf4be57b301; this local repair additionally prevents partial programming.
Retain every surrounding author, license and source notice. Do not infer
hardware acceptance from this new failure-path qualification.

Codex prepared this new local repair and host qualification. Thirteen
selected native objects pass with nonpermissive CFI on supported ARM,
ARM64 and ARM64 RT profiles; MMCC remains native ARM32 only. Original
source/board attribution is retained. Human review, security review and
DCO remain pending; no sign-off certification or hardware claim is made.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 541e79dd8a8b..925967662fb1 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -499,6 +499,11 @@ static int qcom_iommu_init_domain(struct iommu_domain *domain,
 			}
 			ctx->secure_init = true;
 		}
+	}
+
+	/* Finish all fallible secure setup before programming any context bank. */
+	for (i = 0; i < fwspec->num_ids; i++) {
+		struct qcom_iommu_ctx *ctx = to_ctx(qcom_domain, fwspec->ids[i]);
 
 		/* Secured QSMMU-500/QSMMU-v2 contexts cannot be programmed */
 		if (ctx->secured_ctx) {
@@ -551,7 +556,9 @@ static int qcom_iommu_init_domain(struct iommu_domain *domain,
 
 	return 0;
 out_clear_iommu:
+	free_io_pgtable_ops(pgtbl_ops);
 	qcom_domain->iommu = NULL;
+	qcom_domain->fwspec = NULL;
 out_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&qcom_domain->init_mutex);
 	return ret;
-- 
2.56.0

